WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.290
Clear photos, short case studies, and a free site.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.780
This is the video for module two of Online Portfolio Building.

3
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:19.120
For physical work, the photo is the work, as far as an online viewer is concerned. A great outfit in a dark, blurry photo looks like an average outfit.

4
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:26.020
You do not need a professional camera. A smartphone, window daylight and a sheet of white paper are enough.

5
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.820
Then you will write a short case study, so the viewer understands what you did and why.

6
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.250
And you will put it all on a free website, with one link you can share anywhere.

7
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:47.820
Light is the most important thing. Place the item close to a window, with light coming from the side. Side light shows stitching, beading and icing.

8
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:54.950
Hold a sheet of white paper or a white plate on the dark side to soften the shadows. Keep the background plain.

9
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:04.080
Avoid harsh midday sun, which makes hard shadows. Turn off yellow ceiling bulbs, because mixed light gives strange colours.

10
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:10.420
And do not use the flash. It flattens texture and makes shiny spots on soap, glass or satin.

11
00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:20.120
Wipe the lens first, because finger grease makes photos hazy. Then take an overall shot of the whole item, filling most of the frame.

12
00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:30.140
Next a detail shot, close up on a hem, beadwork or piping. Tap the screen on the item to focus, and move closer instead of zooming.

13
00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.060
Then a scale shot, like a hand holding the item, so the viewer knows its size.

14
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:44.030
Finally an in-use shot: the item worn, served or displayed. Take several of each, and keep the sharpest.

15
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:54.770
When you edit, crop and brighten a little only. If the fabric is wine, it must look wine, not red. No beauty filters on hair or makeup work.

16
00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:10.980
For example, Grace makes bead necklaces in Port Harcourt. At about 10 a.m. she sets a small table by her window, out of direct sun, and curves a white card against the wall. It cost approximately 300 naira.

17
00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.300
She switches off the room bulb and holds a white plate on the shadow side.

18
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:24.340
She shoots the necklace from above, then the clasp and bead pattern close up. Her sister wears it against a plain wall.

19
00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:30.490
She takes 15 photos and keeps the sharpest four. It took about 30 minutes.

20
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:42.370
A photo shows what you made. A case study explains why, how, and what difference it made. About 150 to 300 words is enough for a main piece.

21
00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:53.550
For example, Bisi, a baker in Lagos. Problem: a mother wanted a football cake for 40 children in 4 days, at an outdoor party where buttercream could melt.

22
00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:03.830
Process: Bisi suggested firmer fondant, made the toppers two days ahead to dry hard, and sent a sketch on WhatsApp for approval before baking.

23
00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:13.950
Result: the cake stayed firm through the 3-hour party, and the mother has since ordered two more. A new customer learns all that in under a minute.

24
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:21.860
Google Sites is free with your Gmail account. Go to sites dot google dot com and start a blank site.

25
00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:28.120
Type your name, for example Amaka's Cakes Abuja, and a one-line introduction.

26
00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.470
Add pages for Home, Work, About and Contact.

27
00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:40.840
On the Work page, insert your photos and a text box for each case study. Add a button that says Chat on WhatsApp.

28
00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:50.280
Preview it in phone view, then publish. Check the sharing setting so anyone with the link can view it, or customers cannot open it.

29
00:03:51.530 --> 00:04:04.480
One warning. Some people offer a free website, then ask for your email password, your BVN, or a payment to activate it. That is a scam. The real tools are free to sign up for directly.

30
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:13.860
To remember. Use soft side daylight, no flash and a plain background. Take overall, detail, scale and in-use photos.

31
00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:24.110
Write each case study as problem, process and result, with honest results only. Choose one free main home, check it is shared, and guard your passwords.

32
00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:32.910
Now photograph one piece with the four shots, write case studies for your two strongest pieces, and publish your first page.

33
00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.200
Continue with the lessons below.
